coverage:
I read all five sections in full: introduction, lengths, descent, asymptotic, positivity. I checked these steps in detail:
- the reduction lemma (completion, residue extension, prime filtrations, vanishing);
- the char-p construction of C_D, including the trace-conductor bound O(1/q) and the Hilbert-Kunz/Roberts Frobenius limit;
- the first-average lemma (twisting, and chi(D',E') = a_D a_E chi(D,E) via vanishing);
- prime avoidance for x in Q;
- the Tor bound tau_i = 0 for i > l, using the Koszul splitting K(x;L) = sum L[j]^binom;
- the finite-length approximation lemma (sup/inf properties, descent to S_j, locality of S_j, the generator bound);
- the support of truncated resolutions (the degree-l homotopy error is a chain map that factors through the rank-o(s_n) term F_{l+1}[l]);
- the identification of the ordinary evaluation with c_sigma (tail replacement);
- the C_E-evaluation forcing b_i = 0 for i > 0 and b_0 >= nu*eta;
- the Verdier/idempotent arguments in Section 4 (fullness and faithfulness of the supported subquotient, homological functors);
- the formal steps of the descent theorem (truncating E, the support identification, finite-flat retract, flattening induction, orbit/section blowup square);
- consistency tests: a trivial plane-curve case, E regular, and DHM norm sums.
I did not verify the mixed-characteristic perfectoid inputs from the CLMST citations (Cor 4.0.4, Props 4.0.10/4.0.14), or the precise hypotheses of the Land-Tamme Appendix B coefficient descent for the non-Noetherian H.
